In a product leasing model for remanufacturing, the manufacturer retains ownership and leases the product to the user for a defined period. At the end of the lease, the product is returned, remanufactured to original specifications, and leased again. The designer should focus on creating products with high durability, ease of disassembly, and modular upgradeability so that the product can be cost-effectively restored to like-new condition between lease cycles. The lease contract itself should include provisions for maintenance, repair, and return conditions.